.TH SDL_calloc 3 "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 FUNCTIONS"
.SH NAME
SDL_calloc \- Allocate a zero-initialized array.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_stdinc.h>
.PP
.BI "void * SDL_calloc(size_t nmemb, size_t size);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
The memory returned by this function must be freed with
.BR SDL_free ()\[char46]
.PP
If either of
.BR nmemb
or
.BR size
is 0, they will both be set to 1\[char46]
.PP
If the allocation is successful, the returned pointer is guaranteed to be aligned to either the
.IR "fundamental alignment"
.BR "" ( alignof(max_align_t)
in C11 and later) or
.BR "2
.IR " sizeof(void " )"
,
whichever is smaller\[char46] Use
.BR SDL_aligned_alloc_zero ()
if you need to allocate memory aligned to an alignment greater than this guarantee\[char46]

.SH FUNCTION PARAMETERS
.TP
.I nmemb
the number of elements in the array\[char46]
.TP
.I size
the size of each element of the array\[char46]
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns a pointer to the allocated array, or NULL if allocation failed\[char46]

.SH THREAD SAFETY
It is safe to call this function from any thread\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This function is available since SDL 3\[char46]2\[char46]0\[char46]

.SH SEE ALSO
.BR SDL_free (3),
.BR SDL_malloc (3),
.BR SDL_realloc (3)
